  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "The current best (config_019, acc=0.639) uses multimodal + multiprofile + pca_n2000 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted. Evidence shows weighted>concat and avgpool>transformer, and that adding image to RNA helps (0.639 vs 0.591). However, the image-only model with resnet50 was very weak (0.208), suggesting the image encoder is a potential bottleneck in the multimodal fusion. Config_025 makes a single-variable change: upgrading the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while keeping all other winning settings (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted). This directly tests whether a stronger, larger pretrained image representation can further improve the multimodal model. With only 2 experiments remaining, exploiting the best-known configuration with the most targeted upgrade is the highest-expected-value choice, and it cleanly isolates the image encoder effect."
}

